The IMAP mailbox pattern given to twisted.mail.imap4.wildcardToRegexp is no longer compiled as regular expression source. Only the IMAP wildcards ``*`` and ``%`` are given any meaning and every other character is matched literally, closing the denial of service reported as GHSA-8pqf-f4m5-798g and making a mailbox whose name contains regular expression syntax selectable by its own name.
